  "causal_classification": {
    "stage_2_verdict": "BC_PARTIAL_CONTRIBUTOR",
    "localization_direction": "TOWARD_TARGET_LOCALIZATION",
    "findings": [
      "Removing the artificial top u_x=0 lateral constraint eliminates severe corner shear stress concentrations (mean |s12| on top boundary drops by 9.3x from 0.1261 MPa to 0.0136 MPa, max |s12| drops from 0.4880 MPa to 0.0475 MPa).",
      "Top boundary error drops by 57.72% (from 2.9157 MPa to 1.2326 MPa), with top-right corner error dropping by 94.45% (from 0.8896 MPa to 0.0494 MPa).",
      "Total Boundary Regions error drops by 48.39% (from 4.7767 MPa to 2.4652 MPa), shrinking boundary error share from 14.54% to 8.59%.",
      "The normalized error footprint for eta >= 10% contracts from a whole-domain span ([0.01, 0.99] x [0.01, 0.99], dx=0.98, dy=0.98) in Historical to a tightly localized crack-tip box ([0.425, 0.547] x [0.447, 0.540], dx=0.122, dy=0.093) in Corrected.",
      "The native 1.0% errorTarget remesh shrinks by 15,783 elements (-21.89%, from 72,085 to 56,302 finite elements), confirming that top lateral constraint was a substantial parasitic contributor.",
      "However, the corrected 1.0% remesh (56,302 FE) remains 4.04x denser than the published 13,941-element baseline because Far Field error still carries 56.98% of domain error (16.3553 MPa), leading UNIFORM_ERROR sizing to refine broadly.",
      "Therefore, BC implementation is a BC_PARTIAL_CONTRIBUTOR (TOWARD_TARGET_LOCALIZATION), not the complete root-cause closure. The investigation advances to Stage 3 (Abaqus RemeshingRule & Sizing Parameter Mapping)."
    ],
    "next_governed_action": "Advance cause audit to Stage 3: Abaqus RemeshingRule Formulation & Sizing Parameter Mapping."
